{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"7ebef90aebdae1aaf8c05e04d628fe0abe61bbbe14064247bca1bcda0b4ab6ef","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar tracker-footprint command","key_entities":["footprint.py","_pack_layer","measure_tracker","tracker_footprint.py","_render_text","pack_layer schema","DEFINITIONS[\"pack\"]","git clone --shared","alternates","tests/unit/commands/test_tracker_footprint.py","st_blocks","shared_reasons"],"problem_keywords":["footprint measurement","pack layer","shared clone","alternates","completeness","allocation reporting","test coverage","edge cases"],"propositions":["The pack layer measures only the primary common Git object database and cannot distinguish between exclusive object stores and alternates-backed shared clones, creating potential misinterpretation of footprint reports.","The allocation-unavailable text rendering path and CLI bad-argument (argparse) exit-2 path lack direct test coverage.","Allocation assertions depend on a filesystem block-policy assumption (checkout_allocated > pack_logical * 4) that fails on block-suballocating or tail-packing filesystems.","A pack layer boolean field 'complete' is required to explicitly mark whether measured .pack files represent the complete object store backing the checkout or are incomplete due to borrowed alternate object databases."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787607782087038001,"uuid":"25e6d88a-2907-4aed-8cdd-11369cb39b36"}